.vscode/
# The Eclipse JDT language server — the Java extension in VS Code-based editors — imports the
# Gradle module and mirrors its source sets into bin/main and bin/test. JDT does not compile
# Kotlin, so it treats every .kt as a resource and copies it verbatim: the result is a
# byte-identical duplicate of src/, which is build output that happens to look like source.
# Gradle writes to build/ and never reads this, so deleting bin/ is always safe.
bin/

